From b55471f21dd5031d5001c17bfec7c65dcdf953f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zixuan Zhang <zixuan.zhang.uj@renesas.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:26:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] drm: rz-du: hand the running display over to the CM33
 (LowPower Display demo)

The CM33 firmware of the RZ/G3L LowPower Display demo can drive the
running VSPD from a display list in on-chip SRAM, so that the LCDC does
not read DDR any more. Add the Linux side of the hand-over:

- lp_display (sysfs, "linux" | "cm33"): rzg2l_du_lpdemo_enter() waits
  for the last page flip, turns the vblank off and asks the CM33 to take
  the display over through the shared control block;
  rzg2l_du_lpdemo_leave() asks for (or acknowledges) the return and turns
  the vblank back on.
- While the CM33 owns the display, atomic_check refuses every commit
  with -EBUSY.

User space has to stop the compositor first. The same functions are used
by the system suspend path in the next step.
